# A cycle in the extension hierarchy closed through a disjunction: :S
# EXTENDS :Any, and :Any is a choice that names :S.  Neither EXTENDS names
# a shape that EXTENDS it, so the cycle is only visible by following the
# reference out of the choice.
#
# This is the shape of a real schema: FHIR's <Resource> is a choice over
# every resource type, and each of those EXTENDS <DomainResource>, which
# EXTENDS <Resource>.
#
# The extension hierarchy graph MUST be acyclic (Acyclic Extension
# Requirement).
PREFIX :       <http://example.org/>

:Any @:S OR @:T
:S EXTENDS @:Any { :p . }
:T EXTENDS @:Any { :q . }
